  "unreadable": [],
  "notes": "Image shows the Noise Nugget 2040 DevKit v3.0 (silkscreen) with callouts 1-68 running counter-clockwise around the four socket headers; callout numbers used as positions per header. Pin 10 callout is partly cut off at the image top but legible. Board silkscreen on the header holes is mostly too blurry to read reliably and was not transcribed. Skipped MIDI/headset/line TRS jacks, Boot/Reset buttons, USB-C, the unlabeled 'debug' connector, and the prototyping grid. Speaker terminal labels are small silkscreen (R-, R+, L-, L+).",
  "uncertain": [
    "bottom-header positions 1-9 (callouts 35-43): callout labels run GP8..GP16 left to right, but the board silkscreen under these holes reads GPIO16, GPIO15 ... GPIO9, GPIO8 left to right; the label-to-hole mapping for these nine pins is in conflict.",
    "right-header positions 2-3 (callouts 55 Left In 2, 56 Right In 2): board silkscreen reads IN2R then IN2L going upward, the reverse of the callout labels.",
    "Prototyping area columns labeled VIN/GND and 3V3/GND (and the hole grid below the bottom header) were not transcribed; unclear whether they should count as wiring connectors."
  ]
}